statement=standing+('For every deterministic n≥0 let H_n(w)=(R_j(ε(w)))_(0≤j≤n)∈Hist_n=D^(Fin(n+1)), and let μ_n=(H_n)_*P. Thus the last record R_n consumes only raw clocks k<n, and w_n is the next unused clock. Take any Borel function d:Hist_n→[0,∞); each d(h) is finite but the function need not be bounded. Define L(r,u,e) to mean u<τ_z(max(e,0)) when r=live(T,z), and false when r=stopped. Define q(r,u)=exp(−Λ_z(u)) when r=live(T,z), and zero when r=stopped. The event B_d={(h,v)∈Hist_n×ℝ^ℕ:L(h_n,d(h),v_0)} is Borel. The weight q_d(h)=q(h_n,d(h)) is Borel and 0≤q_d(h)≤1 for every history h. For every Borel A⊆Hist_n, P{w:H_n(w)∈A and L(R_n(ε(w)),d(H_n(w)),w_n)}=∫_A q_d(h) μ_n(dh). All conclusions hold for every deterministic y,r,z₀,n and admissible d,A under the same six standing analytic hypotheses. No positivity of μ_n(A), boundedness of d, finite-wait assumption or extra regularity/independence/conditional-law provider is required. Live histories whose next wait is infinite survive every finite d(h); stopped histories have zero weight and no fictitious phase or wait in the statement. The case n=0, null events, zero rates and dimension zero are included. Borel d and A specify admissible deterministic tests rather than additional analytic hypotheses. This is an attributed ASTIS completion of the history-dependent conditional survival ingredient implicit in AppendixA.1(A.7), using the actual recursion. Conditional finite-wait densities, ordered-time disintegration and iteration, final path factor assembly, full(A.7), physical-time residual memorylessness, random stopping/restart/Markovness, reversal, invariance, all-L² contraction, implementation error/cost, main results and actual-input composition remain separate obligations.')
assumptions=['E is finite-dimensional over ℝ with inner product and its Borel structure, including rank zero. V:E→ℝ is C².','The six original analytic hypotheses are α>0, α≤β, V∈C², α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v, η>0, and βη≤1; α,β≥0.','y,r,z₀ and event depth n are deterministic and universally quantified. P and the actual stopped recursion are literal definitions.','d is any Borel finite-valued nonnegative duration function of the whole finite history; A is any Borel history event. These classify test objects. d may be unbounded and μ_n(A) may vanish.','No state measurability, independence, regular conditional law, density or integrability estimate is supplied as a premise. Stopped records are guarded; live infinite waits and zero rates are permitted.']
formulae=[r'H_n=(R_0,\ldots,R_n),\quad\mu_n=(H_n)_*P,\quad d:\operatorname{Hist}_n\to[0,\infty)\text{ Borel}.',r'L(r,u,e)=\begin{cases}u<\tau_z(\max(e,0)),&r=\operatorname{live}(T,z),\\\mathrm{false},&r=\mathrm{stopped},\end{cases}\quad q(r,u)=\begin{cases}e^{-\Lambda_z(u)},&r=\operatorname{live}(T,z),\\0,&r=\mathrm{stopped}.\end{cases}',r'B_d\in\mathcal B(\operatorname{Hist}_n\times\mathbb R^{\mathbb N}),\quad q_d\text{ Borel},\quad0\le q_d\le1.',r'P\{H_n\in A,\ L(R_n,d(H_n),w_n)\}=\int_A q(h_n,d(h))\,\mu_n(dh).']
