steps=[
step('Keep actual definitions and consume verified producers','Retain the actual flow, reflection, intensity, integrated hazard, infinity-guarded crossing recursion and independent Exp(1) input. The existing hazard-clock theorem supplies joint Borel Λ and τ, nonnegative Λ and deterministic-state survival. The exponential-product theorem supplies P probability and each coordinate law. The finite-history theorem supplies Borel H_n,Y_n and their exact joint law μ_n⊗P. Its raw tail Y_n starts at n, hence Y_n(w)_0=w_n. None of these ingredients is an added premise.',r'(H_n,Y_n)_*P=\mu_n\otimes P,\qquad Y_n(w)_0=w_n.','  classical\n','  -- A stopped record'),
step('Derive the joint survival event measurability','Distribute the Borel record sum across the raw clock coordinate. On live records the wait observable is the composition of the joint Borel τ with the phase projection and e↦max(e,0); on the stopped summand use the zero observable solely for this proof. Since u≥0, u<0 is false, so this auxiliary observable gives exactly L, never a new stopped phase or algorithm transition. Compose with the Borel last-history projection, d and tail coordinate0. Strict comparison in [0,∞] is Borel, proving B_d is Borel.',r'L(r,u,e)\iff u<\operatorname{waitObs}(r,e),\qquad u\ge0.','  -- A stopped record','  -- Joint Borel hazard'),
step('Derive the Borel bounded survival weight','Distribute the record sum across duration. On the live summand joint Borel Λ followed by x↦exp(−x) and inclusion into the extended nonnegative reals is Borel; on the stopped summand the weight is zero. Compose with h↦(h_n,d(h)). Nonnegativity Λ_z(u)≥0 gives exp(−Λ_z(u))≤1. Thus every q_d(h) lies in [0,1], even when d as a function is unbounded. This bound is derived internally.',r'\Lambda_z(u)\ge0\Longrightarrow0\le e^{-\Lambda_z(u)}\le1.','  -- Joint Borel hazard','  -- For every fixed live history'),
step('Evaluate each fixed-history survival fiber','Fix a history h. For a stopped last record the fiber is empty and its P-measure is zero. For a live last record z, push raw coordinate0 forward under P to Exp(1), then push that law through e↦τ_z(max(e,0)). The existing hazard-clock theorem identifies the real probability of (d(h),∞] with exp(−Λ_z(d(h))). Its pushed law is a probability measure, so conversion to an extended nonnegative measure loses no mass. This is a pointwise identity for every fixed h and its d(h), not substitution into separate almost-everywhere statements indexed by fixed times.',r'P\{v:L(h_n,d(h),v_0)\}=q_d(h)\quad\text{for every }h.','  -- For every fixed live history','  refine ⟨hB, hw, hbound'),
step('Integrate over the actual history law without normalization','For Borel A let C={(h,v):h∈A and (h,v)∈B_d}, a Borel product-space event. Its pullback under (H_n,Y_n) is exactly the desired actual-clock event. Replace the pushforward by μ_n⊗P and apply the product-measure section formula. The section has mass q_d(h) on A and zero off A. Its integral is the integral of the indicator of A times q_d, hence ∫_A q_d dμ_n. No division by μ_n(A), regular conditional distribution or bounded duration assumption enters.',formulae[3],'  refine ⟨hB, hw, hbound','\nend\n')]
assert ''.join(x['lean'] for x in steps)==s[body:s.index('\nend\n',body)]
